            <ArticleTitle>Multiple myeloma: short T2 on MR imaging.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>141-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a rare case of multiple myeloma with marked hypointense areas on both T1- and T2-weighted images. Amyloid deposition and calcification were not found histologically. Hypointensity on T2-weighted images may be caused by distributed free radicals produced by significant macrophages.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
